.TH FL-CLIPHIST 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-cliphist \- clipboard history
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-cliphist\fR
.br
\fBfl-cliphist\fR \fB\-\-list\fR | \fB\-\-copy\fR \fIID\fR | \fB\-\-set\fR \fITEXT\fR | \fB\-\-set\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR | \fB\-\-paste\fR
.br
\fBfl-cliphist\fR \fB\-\-pin\fR \fIID\fR | \fB\-\-unpin\fR \fIID\fR | \fB\-\-delete\fR \fIID\fR | \fB\-\-clear\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without options, \fBfl-cliphist\fR records what is copied, through the
wlr-data-control protocol of \fBfl-wm\fR(1): texts (as UTF-8) and PNG images,
up to 32 MB each. The session starts it
(\fI/etc/xdg/autostart/fl-cliphist.desktop\fR). Copying the same thing again
moves it to the top. Copies marked by password managers
(x-kde-passwordManagerHint) are not recorded.
.PP
The clipboard button of \fBfl-panel\fR(1) lists the history; clicking an
entry puts it on the clipboard again, entries can be pinned (kept when the
history is cleared or full) and removed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
The history, newest first: id, P for pinned, type and a preview, separated
by tabs.
.TP
\fB\-\-copy\fR \fIID\fR
Put an entry on the clipboard; a background process offers it until
something else is copied.
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fITEXT\fR, \fB\-\-set\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
Put a text, or a file's contents (a PNG file as an image), on the clipboard.
.TP
\fB\-\-paste\fR
Print the text on the clipboard.
.TP
\fB\-\-pin\fR, \fB\-\-unpin\fR, \fB\-\-delete\fR \fIID\fR; \fB\-\-clear\fR
Pin, unpin or remove an entry; remove all but the pinned ones.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/fldesktop/clipboard/\fR
The history (\fB$XDG_STATE_HOME\fR).
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/panel.ini\fR
\fB[Clipboard]\fR: \fBHistory=false\fR stops recording, \fBMax=\fR (50) is the
number of unpinned entries kept, \fBButton=false\fR hides the panel button.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-panel\fR(1), \fBfl-wm\fR(1)
